    "title": "Aaron Jones Week 3 Preview vs. the Buccaneers - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago Photo: Geoff Stellfox / Getty Images Sport / Getty Images Minnesota Vikings running back Aaron Jones has a difficult matchup in Week 3 (Sunday at 4:05 p.m. ET), playing the Tampa Bay Buccaneers. The Buccaneers are conceding the fourth-fewest rushing yards in the NFL, 75 per game.\nJones has amassed a team-best 145 rushing yards on 35 attempts (72.5 ypg) this season, including one rushing TD.\nListen to the game on KFAN FM 100.3 Jones vs. the Buccaneers Jones vs the Buccaneers (since 2021): 3 GP / 20.7 RUSH YPG / 2 RUSH TD The Buccaneers have not allowed 100 or more yards to an opposing rusher in the 2026 season. Tampa Bay has given up one or more rushing TDs to one opposing player this year. The Buccaneers have not given up more than one rushing TD to an opposing player this season. The Buccaneers yield 75 rushing yards per game, the NFL's fourth-ranked run defense this season. So far this season, the Buccaneers have allowed one passing TDs to opponents, averaging 0.5 per game. That ranks ninth among NFL defenses. Catch NFL action all year long on Fubo.\nJones Rushing Insights The Vikings, who are 15th in NFL play in points scored, have passed 41.5% of the time while running 58.5%. He has handled 56.5% of his team's 62 rushing attempts this season (35). Jones has rushed for a touchdown once this season in two games played. He has one touchdown this season (20.0% of his team's five offensive TDs). He has four red zone carries for 50.0% of the team share (his team runs on 61.5% of its plays in the red zone). Get in the game and sign up for FanDuel Fantasy today. Use our link to start playing daily fantasy.\nJones' Recent Performance Opponent Date Week Rushing Stats Receiving Stats vs. Bears 9/20/2026 Week 2 23 ATT / 105 YDS / 0 TDs TAR / 0 REC / 0 YDS / 0 TDs vs. Packers 9/13/2026 Week 1 12 ATT / 40 YDS / 1 TD 1 TAR / 0 REC / 0 YDS / 0 TDs",
